#13500
Labyrinth: Oubliette~
   You awaken in an unfamiliar place. The walls and floor are cold stone. The
ceiling is so high you cannot see the chute that dropped you here, at least,
not in the dark. You've really done it this time.
   A drip echoes in the distance. A shuffle. Perhaps a scurry. And a creak. A
long moment of silence, broken by the sound of pottery shattering, echoing back
and forth. And then silence again.
   And then a voice.
   What is this place?
~
   Relief washes over you as you press yourself through the tight passage and
it opens into such a grand chamber. But it's brief. The exit is blocked by the
minotaur.
~
