#13501
Labyrinth: Descent~
   You cast a glance upward to the chute, now so high above that you can't make
it out in the dark. The walls are cold stone, stretching out into the darkness
in each direction. A drip echoes from the distance; you can't tell which way it
came from as it echoes back again.
   Then it's silent.
   A scurrying sound. A creak.
   Then more silence.
   No one would bury a place as impressive as this if there isn't something
grand hidden down here.
   But it seems you aren't the first to find it.
~
   You press yourself through the tight passage and it opens into a grand
chamber. It took some work, but it looks like you've found the center. There's
just the minotaur between you and the ladder.
~
