#13512
Labyrinth: Return of the Nightmare Queen~
   The Nightmare Queen is real... and she is risen!
   This is the point in the story where the rational adventurer would be
reconsidering their actions. Each seal has been broken with little thought as
to why they were sealed. Now, the ancient abomination stands over you -- and
if the flames are any indication, she is mad.
   As the one who unleashed her on this world, it falls to you to find a way
to put her back in the jar. Or, barring that, find some other way to stop her.
The lid is smashed and broken on the floor. Worse, the Nightmare Queen blocks
the exit. Whatever you're going to do, you're on your own.
   Once it's done, seek out the priest in the temple above.
~
   The priest listens intently, hands folded, as you weave the tale of the
Nightmare Queen, once sealed away, then accidentally released.
   'I had never heard the legend,' the priest says. 'Who knew such an ancient
evil was buried right beneath our feet. It's lucky the temple is here to
contain it, or she might have escaped. But how did you defeat her?'
   You continue the tale, recounting every detail of the fiery battle from
which you narrowly emerged victorious. The priest hangs on your every word.
   'I would have liked to see it for myself, risk of death be damned,' he says
when the story draws to a close. 'I used to be an adventurer like you, you
know. Until I took an arrow to the knee.'
   The priest thanks you for the story, promising to commit it to parchment for
posterity. He then excuses himself and returns to his duties, still musing over
the epic tale.
   A glint of gold catches your eye. You're not sure where it came from, but a
young horse is following you, gleaming golden in the light.
~
