#13526
Labyrinth: See You On The Other Side~
   The fuzzy goblin scratches behind her ear and checks herself all over before
thanking you for the rescue.
   'Not gonna lie,' she says. 'Most harrowing experience of my entire life. And
I've been through plenty. Could tell you some stories... but not here. Ghost
the nasty minotaur and meet up again outside.'
~
   You find the fuzzy goblin resting on a large beam up in the rafters,
catching her breath. She leans back and nibbles at a bit of moldy cheese.
   'All started with a woman,' she says as she licks her fingers. 'Yeah, yeah,
same old story, I know. But here we are. Honestly thought I'd be a rat forever.
Despite all my rage, trapped like a rat in a... well, you know.'
   She brushes her green-tinged fur with her fingernails, trying to smooth down
spots that seem to have a mind of their own. She looks up at you.
   'Guess the spell hasn't worn off completely, and me having a bad fur day.
Not my worst day, though. If I ever catch the rat that turned me...' she looks
around at the temple. 'If he's even still alive. Don't know how long I was a
rat. Before that, I was Cherrith. Used to be a Goblin King...
   'Had it all, gold, silver, copper, fame, adoring followers, even my own
labby.... But there was a woman. Something about her. She was different, wasn't
just some sewer babe; she the babe with the power, let me tell you. Any-who,
the crew didn't want her around because she was, well, you know...'
   The goblin scratches behind her ear.
   'She was a human. They kept calling me Pinko. Stabbed more than a few of
them but was losin' follower left, right, and under. Pretty soon I hear some
other goblin casting a spell and BAM! Rats...
   'Couldn't even be Rat King on account of I can't dance.'
   She pauses and looks up at you.
   'Craziest thing you ever hear, right? No more labbies for me. Don't think
I can go back to being Goblin King, neither. Maybe I can find Babe, though.
Human luck to you, friend-o. Or whatever you say.'
~
